[2.5px]" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57="true" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="M12 5v14"></path></svg> </span> </summary> <p class="mt-5 pr-4 sm:pr-16 text-base text-gray-600 leading-[1.85]" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> It targets supported Gemini and Veo-style visible video watermarks. For best results, test with a short Veo 3 clip first. </p> </details><details class="group py-5 sm:py-8" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-6 list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> <span class="text-[16px] sm:text-[19px] font-bold text-gray-900" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> Is this a free Gemini video watermark remover? </span> <span class="flex h-10 w-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg transition-colors bg-gray-100 text-gray-400 group-open:bg-gray-950 group-open:text-white" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> <svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-[18px] w-[18px] transition-transform group-open:rotate-45 stroke-[2.5px]" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57="true" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="M12 5v14"></path></svg> </span> </summary> <p class="mt-5 pr-4 sm:pr-16 text-base text-gray-600 leading-[1.85]" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> Yes for supported Gemini and Veo-style files, including a Gemini video download without watermark after local export. It is not a general-purpose video watermark remover; for other logos, captions, or platform marks, use the Pilio fallback. </p> </details><details class="group py-5 sm:py-8" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-6 list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> <span class="text-[16px] sm:text-[19px] font-bold text-gray-900" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> Are my videos uploaded? </span> <span class="flex h-10 w-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg transition-colors bg-gray-100 text-gray-400 group-open:bg-gray-950 group-open:text-white" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> <svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-[18px] w-[18px] transition-transform group-open:rotate-45 stroke-[2.5px]" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57="true" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="M12 5v14"></path></svg> </span> </summary> <p class="mt-5 pr-4 sm:pr-16 text-base text-gray-600 leading-[1.85]" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> No. The browser tool runs locally. Your video file stays on your device. </p> </details><details class="group py-5 sm:py-8" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-6 list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> <span class="text-[16px] sm:text-[19px] font-bold text-gray-900" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> Is video cleanup as stable as image cleanup? </span> <span class="flex h-10 w-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg transition-colors bg-gray-100 text-gray-400 group-open:bg-gray-950 group-open:text-white" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> <svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-[18px] w-[18px] transition-transform group-open:rotate-45 stroke-[2.5px]" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57="true" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="M12 5v14"></path></svg> </span> </summary> <p class="mt-5 pr-4 sm:pr-16 text-base text-gray-600 leading-[1.85]" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> Not yet. Image cleanup is the mature default path. Video cleanup is a newer local workflow, best tested on short supported Gemini videos first. </p> </details><details class="group py-5 sm:py-8" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-6 list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> <span class="text-[16px] sm:text-[19px] font-bold text-gray-900" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> What should I use for large videos? </span> <span class="flex h-10 w-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg transition-colors bg-gray-100 text-gray-400 group-open:bg-gray-950 group-open:text-white" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> <svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-[18px] w-[18px] transition-transform group-open:rotate-45 stroke-[2.5px]" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57="true" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="M12 5v14"></path></svg> </span> </summary> <p class="mt-5 pr-4 sm:pr-16 text-base text-gray-600 leading-[1.85]" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> Use the CLI. It gives more control over timeouts and is easier to repeat for larger local files. </p> </details> </div> </div> </div> </section> <!-- CTA --> <section class="relative py-16 sm:py-24 md:py-32 overflow-hidden" style="background: linear-gradient(to bottom, #091024 0%, #284c7e 45%, #6e9ed5 75%, #bedcf8 100%);" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> <div class="container relative z-10 text-center" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-white md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl leading-tight" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> Ready to clean your<br data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57>Gemini videos? </h2> <p class="mx-auto mt-4 sm:mt-5 max-w-xl text-base sm:text-lg text-white/70" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> Process supported Gemini and Veo 3 video watermarks locally and download a clean MP4 — free, private, and open source. </p> <div class="mt-8 sm:mt-10 flex flex-col sm:flex-row flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3 sm:gap-4 px-4 sm:px-0" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> <a href="#video-tool" class="inline-flex w-full sm:w-auto items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-white px-8 py-3.5 text-base font-semibold text-gray-950 shadow-lg transition hover:bg-gray-100" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> Remove Gemini video watermark <svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="ml-2 h-5 w-5" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57="true" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg> </a> <a href="https://github.com/GargantuaX/gemini-watermark-remover" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex w-full sm:w-auto items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-white/15 px-8 py-3.5 text-base font-semibold text-white backdrop-blur transition hover:bg-white/25" data-astro-cid-7jsw6l57> View on GitHub </a> </div> </div> </section> </main> <script>(function(){const hardwareInfoTpl = "{cores} cores · {memory}";
const copyLinkDoneText = "Link copied!";

    (function detectMobileDevice() {
      // Skip if user already dismissed in this session
      var wasDismissed = false;
      try {
        wasDismissed =
          sessionStorage.getItem("gwr-mobile-overlay-dismissed") === "1";
      } catch {
        wasDismissed = false;
      }
      if (wasDismissed) return;

      var ua = navigator.userAgent || "";
      var isMobileUA =
        /Android|webOS|iPhone|iPad|iPod|BlackBerry|IEMobile|Opera Mini|Mobile|mobile/i.test(
          ua,
        );
      var hasTouchOnly =
        ("ontouchstart" in window || navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0) &&
        !window.matchMedia("(pointer: fine)").matches;
      var cores = navigator.hardwareConcurrency || 0;
      var memory = navigator.deviceMemory || 0; // deviceMemory is Chrome-only, returns GB

      // Consider it "mobile" if UA says mobile, or if it's a touch-only device with low resources
      var isLikelyMobile =
        isMobileUA || (hasTouchOnly && (cores <= 4 || memory <= 4));

      if (!isLikelyMobile) return;

      var overlay = document.getElementById("mobile-device-overlay");
      var badge = document.getElementById("mobile-hw-badge");
      var dismissBtn = document.getElementById("mobile-overlay-dismiss");
      var closeBtn = document.getElementById("mobile-overlay-close");
      var copyBtn = document.getElementById("mobile-overlay-copy");
      if (!overlay) return;

      // Show hardware info badge if we can detect anything
      if (badge && (cores > 0 || memory > 0)) {
        var memoryText = memory > 0 ? memory + " GB RAM" : "RAM unknown";
        var coresText = cores > 0 ? String(cores) : "?";
        badge.textContent = hardwareInfoTpl
          .replace("{cores}", coresText)
          .replace("{memory}", memoryText);
        badge.classList.remove("hidden");
      }

      // Show the overlay
      overlay.classList.remove("hidden");
      overlay.classList.add("is-visible");
      document.body.style.overflow = "hidden";

      // Dismiss handler function
      function dismissOverlay() {
        overlay.classList.add("is-dismissing");
        try {
          sessionStorage.setItem("gwr-mobile-overlay-dismissed", "1");
        } catch {
          // Storage may be disabled; dismissal still works for this page view.
        }
        setTimeout(function () {
          overlay.classList.remove("is-visible", "is-dismissing");
          overlay.classList.add("hidden");
          document.body.style.overflow = "";
        }, 250);
      }

      if (dismissBtn) dismissBtn.addEventListener("click", dismissOverlay);
      if (closeBtn) closeBtn.addEventListener("click", dismissOverlay);

      // Copy link handler
      if (copyBtn) {
        copyBtn.addEventListener("click", function () {
          var url = window.location.href;
          if (navigator.clipboard && navigator.clipboard.writeText) {
            navigator.clipboard
              .writeText(url)
              .then(function () {
                var textSpan = document.getElementById("copy-btn-text");
                if (textSpan) {
                  var originalText =
                    textSpan.dataset.orig || textSpan.textContent;
                  textSpan.dataset.orig = originalText;
                  textSpan.textContent = copyLinkDoneText;
                  copyBtn.classList.add(
                    "text-green-600",
                    "border-green-200",
                    "bg-green-50",
                  );
                  copyBtn.classList.remove("text-gray-700", "border-gray-100");
                  setTimeout(function () {
                    textSpan.textContent = originalText;
                    copyBtn.classList.remove(
                      "text-green-600",
                      "border-green-200",
                      "bg-green-50",
                    );
                    copyBtn.classList.add("text-gray-700", "border-gray-100");
                  }, 2000);
                }
              })
              .catch(function () {
                // Clipboard writes can be blocked by browser policy.
              });
          }
        });
      }
    })();
